# New session workspace name collision

When a new repo-backed session would create a workspace whose name already
exists, the workspace name is disambiguated before rendering and creation. The
session name and workspace path are both derived from the disambiguated name.

Capture the physical sandbox root once to normalize workspace paths.

    :b jj tmux sed pwd (available)
    :$ -q pwd -P (exit: 0)
    := ROOT (bound)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ -q jj git init beta (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj workspace add -R beta --name zeta beta.zeta (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj describe -R beta -m "beta commit" (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r beta" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 10 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Select the default repo, set it as the current repo context, then type the name
of an existing sibling workspace.

    :k beta C-r C-u zeta
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: zeta
  0/3 | [C-r] repo: ~/beta, [C-o] onto: trunk()
▌  beta/zeta~1                              ~/beta.zeta~1                                                    workspace ┃

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt default@ hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) beta commit
│ ○  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt zeta@ hhhhhhhh
├─╯  (empty) (no description set)
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh
```

    :t set-hook -g client-session-changed "set-hook -gu client-session-changed; wait-for -S created-session" (success)
    :k enter
    :t wait-for created-session (success)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Accepting the row should create and switch to the disambiguated workspace.

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
beta/zeta~1
```

    :t list-sessions -F '#{session_name}:#{b:@smth.repo}' (success)

```
beta/zeta~1:beta.zeta~1
runner:
```

    :$ jj workspace list -R beta --no-pager --color never --template 'name ++ "\t" ++ root ++ "\n"' (exit: 0)
    :| sed "s#${ROOT}/##g" (exit: 0)

```stdout
default	beta
zeta	beta.zeta
"zeta~1"	beta.zeta~1
```

